You are helping build UIPilot — a Unity Editor automation tool 
built in C# for Unity 6.3 LTS (6000.3.11f1).

═══════════════════════════════════════════
WHAT IS UIPILOT
═══════════════════════════════════════════
A Unity Editor-time automation tool that generates, wires, 
validates and repairs standard Unity UGUI systems.
Zero runtime footprint. No custom frameworks. No monoliths.
All output is standard native Unity UI editable by the developer.

═══════════════════════════════════════════
STACK
═══════════════════════════════════════════
- Unity 6.3 LTS (6000.3.11f1)
- Built-In Render Pipeline
- UGUI only (UI Toolkit module planned for future)
- C# Editor scripting only
- TextMeshPro for all text elements

═══════════════════════════════════════════
ARCHITECTURE RULES — NEVER BREAK THESE
═══════════════════════════════════════════
- No runtime MonoBehaviours ever
- No hardcoded strings — all strings in Labels/Content files
- No logic inside UIPilotWindow.cs — UI layer only
- Modules never call each other except via UIPilotWindow, or via
  UIPilotHealthMonitor, the one coordinator that runs with the window
  closed (approved 2026-09-19). Nothing else may call a module.
- Scope: UIPilot may READ any UI in the scene (UI Health), but may
  CHANGE an object that is not UIPilot_ only when the developer clicks
  that row's Fix, as one undoable step. Checks never modify a scene.
- Unity internals: only UIPilotToolbarLamp may use one (the internal
  MainToolbar.TryGetOverlay, to show the toolbar lamp; approved
  2026-09-19). Look it up by reflection, guard every call, and keep
  a public fallback (written instructions). Nowhere else.
- UI Health must not cry wolf: report only what is certain. A check
  that would guess (draw order across nested or camera canvases,
  runtime-only state) stays silent instead.
- Single responsibility per class
- No over-abstraction — only build what is asked
- Always compile with zero errors before finishing
- Ask before refactoring anything not requested
- Minimal code — no bloat, no unnecessary classes

═══════════════════════════════════════════
FOLDER STRUCTURE
═══════════════════════════════════════════
Assets/UIPilot/Editor/
  Core/
    UIPilotLabels.cs
    UIPilotEventSystem.cs   (the only place an EventSystem is created —
                             picks the input module for the project)
    UIPilotSceneQuery.cs    (finds canvas children incl. inactive ones)
    UIPilotTheme.cs         (ScriptableObject: every colour, size and
                             decoration switch of the generated menus)
  Modules/
    UIGenerator/
      MenuType.cs
      UIGeneratorContent.cs
      UIGeneratorModule.cs
      UIGeneratorMenuBuilder.cs   (STRUCTURE only — never sets a look)
      UIGeneratorStyler.cs        (the ONLY code that sets appearance;
                                   used by Build UI and Apply Theme)
      UIGeneratorThemePresets.cs  (Soft Club, Soft Club Night, Ink)
      UIGeneratorArt.cs           (finds the shipped sprites and font)
    Health/                 (UI Health: read-only checks of ANY UI)
      HealthModule.cs       (entry: CheckOpenScenes, CheckSceneForBuild, RunFix)
      HealthScope.cs        (gathers scene objects once per run)
      HealthEventChecks.cs  (click events, EventSystem)
      HealthRaycastChecks.cs  (raycasters, blocked buttons)
      HealthHandheldChecks.cs (gamepad navigation, Steam Deck text size)
      HealthCheck.cs / HealthSeverity.cs / HealthIssue.cs
      HealthContent.cs / HealthSettings.cs (per user, UserSettings/)
    ActionDiscovery/
      DiscoveredAction.cs
      ActionDiscoveryModule.cs
    Binding/
      BindingContent.cs
      BindingModule.cs
    Validation/
      ValidationSeverity.cs
      ValidationResult.cs
      ValidationContent.cs
      ValidationModule.cs
  UI/
    UIPilotStyles.cs        (cached GUIStyles, colours, GUILayoutOptions —
                             never build a GUIStyle inside OnGUI)
    UIPilotToolbarLamp.cs   (UI Health lamp on Unity's main toolbar)
    UIPilotHierarchyLamps.cs (UI Health lamps in the Hierarchy)
  UIPilotWindow.cs
  UIPilotWindow.Health.cs   (the UI Health section, partial class)
  UIPilotHealthMonitor.cs   (coordinator: runs checks, window open or not)
  UIPilotHealthBuildCheck.cs (IProcessSceneWithReport: warns per build scene)
Assets/UIPilot/Art/       (white tintable sprites + Michroma font, shipped)
Assets/UIPilot/Themes/    (the preset theme assets buyers pick from)

═══════════════════════════════════════════
DESIGN SYSTEM — READ BEFORE ANY VISUAL CHANGE
═══════════════════════════════════════════
design-system/uipilot/MASTER.md is the source of truth for how
the generated menus AND the UIPilot window look: colour tokens,
type scale, 8-point spacing, components, states, accessibility.
- Follow it. Do not invent colours, sizes or a second accent.
- No placeholder copy, ever: every string shows real project
  data or does real work.
- A visual change is not done until it has been rendered in
  Unity and looked at (MASTER.md section 9).
- If the design itself should change, change MASTER.md first.
- The menu look is a UIPilotTheme asset. A theme never changes
  structure; all styling goes through UIGeneratorStyler.Apply.
  Rules: design-system/uipilot/pages/generated-menus.md, "Themes".

═══════════════════════════════════════════
NAMING CONVENTIONS
═══════════════════════════════════════════
Generated Unity objects:
  Canvas:   UIPilot_Canvas (always singular in scene)
  Panels:   UIPilot_MainMenu_Panel
            UIPilot_PauseMenu_Panel
            UIPilot_Settings_Panel
  Titles:   UIPilot_MainMenu_Title etc
  Buttons:  UIPilot_Btn_Play
            UIPilot_Btn_Settings
            UIPilot_Btn_Quit
            UIPilot_Btn_Resume
            UIPilot_Btn_Back

Script objects:
  UIPilot_GameManager (GameObject)
  UIPilot_GameManager.cs (script)

═══════════════════════════════════════════
MODULE KNOWLEDGE
═══════════════════════════════════════════
Module 1 — UIGeneratorModule
  Generate(MenuType) — creates Canvas, Panel, TMP, Buttons
  ClearPanel(MenuType) — destroys specific panel only
  Single canvas rule — always reuses UIPilot_Canvas
  Full Undo support on all operations

Module 2 — ActionDiscoveryModule
  Scan() → List<DiscoveredAction>
  BindingFlags.DeclaredOnly — user methods only
  Filters: public, no parameters, not Unity lifecycle
  Assembly guards: IsDynamic + try/catch GetTypes()

Module 3 — BindingModule
  FindUIPilotButtons() → List<Button>
  ApplyBindings(selections, actions)
  Uses UnityEventTools for persistent listeners
  Backwards iteration when removing listeners

Module 4 — ValidationModule
  Validate() → List<ValidationResult>
  RunAutoFix(ValidationResult)
  Re-runs validation immediately after fix
  MarkSceneDirty after all changes

Module 5 — ScriptSetupModule
Entry point: GenerateGameManager(MenuType[])
Output: Assets/UIPilot_GameManager.cs + UIPilot_GameManager GameObject

═══════════════════════════════════════════
EDITOR WINDOW RULES
═══════════════════════════════════════════
- All buttons use pre-cached static readonly GUIContent
- No allocations inside OnGUI
- All state fields null-checked before use
- Sections: Generate, Discover, Wire, Validate
- Workflow guide HelpBox always visible at top
- Contextual HelpBox per section when state is empty

═══════════════════════════════════════════
CODE RULES
═══════════════════════════════════════════
- Always use UnityEngine.Object fully qualified 
  to avoid CS0104 ambiguous reference
- Always null-check state fields before DrawSection methods
- Use GameObject.Find for scene-wide searches
- Use GetComponentsInChildren with (true) to include inactive
- Use StringComparison.Ordinal for name prefix checks
- Use Undo.RecordObject before any scene modifications
- Use EditorSceneManager.MarkSceneDirty after modifications
- Use EditorUtility.SetDirty on modified components

═══════════════════════════════════════════
SCOPE RULES
═══════════════════════════════════════════
- Only read files inside Assets/UIPilot/ unless told otherwise
- Do not touch modules not mentioned in the current task
- Do not add features not requested
- Do not refactor working code unless asked
- Keep changes minimal and targeted

